rting to the Principal Investigator, the RUN2STEM Project Coordinator will provide day to day management support for the RUN2STEM Robert Noyce Teacher Scholarship Program. Examples of Duties SPECIFIC RESPONSIBILITIES Facilitate communication between project participants, including both on- and off-campus stakeholders; Attend on- and off-campus meetings; Participate on the Selection Committee; Coordinate tracking related to the progress and success of each Noyce scholar; Support recruitment and retention initiatives for the Noyce program; Provide support for project programming, including a workshop series; Perform other duties as assigned Qualifications EDUCATION AND QUALIFICATIONS Graduate Assistant must be matriculated and enrolled in a related graduate program and make satisfactory academic progress towards degree completion. Enrollment in a minimum of six (6) credit hours per semester or two (2) courses per semester, whichever is greater, during the academic year (fall and spring semesters). Graduate Assistant shall maintain a minimum grade point average of 3.0 or higher and be in good academic standing as defined by the College or other college/university in which the Graduate Assistant is enrolled. Excellent oral and written communication skills are a must. Experience in undergraduate academic and student affairs services is preferred. Supplemental Information EEO STATEMENT: Ramapo College is an Affirmative Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Ramapo has a long history of advocating, advising, and supporting diversity, equity, and inclusiveness. Examples can be found in its mission statement, strategic plans, degree and course offerings, community outreach programs, and other diversity programs. Ramapo’s commitment to diversity and inclusion is infused across all facets of the College; where the environment is welcoming, dedicated to social justice, respectful of freedom of expression, focused on educating and having an ongoing conversation regarding 